/T (adapters to provide both internet connectivityand isolated communication between the machines.  After configuring the virtual environment, network connectivity was verified by assigning  appropriate IP addresses and testing communication between all systems using ICMP  ping. Once the network was functioning correctly, Wireshark was installed to capture and  analyze network traffic. Different protocols such as ARP, ICMP, DNS, TCP, and HTTPS were  observed to understand how devices communicate over the network.  The next phase of the lab involved deploying the Wazuh SIEM platform on Ubuntu Linux.  After the successful installation of the Wazuh server, agents were installed and configured  on both the Windows and Kali Linux systems. These agents were connected to the Wazuh  manager, allowing the dashboard to receive endpoint logs and security events in real time.  Finally, the Wazuh dashboard was used to verify the connected agents, monitor system  activities, and explore different security monitoring features such as Security Events,  Threat Hunting, and MITRE ATT&CK mapping. By the end of the week, a fully functional SOC  lab environment had been successfully established, providing hands-on experience with  network analysis, endpoint monitoring, and security event management.  Lab Architecture )
/E (adapters to provide both internet connectivityand isolated communication between the machines.  After configuring the virtual environment, network connectivity was verified by assigning  appropriate IP addresses and testing communication between all systems using ICMP  ping. Once the network was functioning correctly, Wireshark was installed to capture and  analyze network traffic. Different protocols such as ARP, ICMP, DNS, TCP, and HTTPS were  observed to understand how devices communicate over the network.  The next phase of the lab involved deploying the Wazuh SIEM platform on Ubuntu Linux.  After the successful installation of the Wazuh server, agents were installed and configured  on both the Windows and Kali Linux systems. These agents were connected to the Wazuh  manager, allowing the dashboard to receive endpoint logs and security events in real time.  Finally, the Wazuh dashboard was used to verify the connected agents, monitor system  activities, and explore different security monitoring features such as Security Events,  Threat Hunting, and MITRE ATT&CK mapping. By the end of the week, a fully functional SOC  lab environment had been successfully established, providing hands-on experience with  network analysis, endpoint monitoring, and security event management.  Lab Architecture )
