/Title (The figure illustrates the overall architecture ofthe virtual cybersecurity laboratory. Ubuntu Linux hosts the Wazuh SIEM server, while Windows and Kali Linux operate as monitored endpoints through Wazuh agents. The Host-Only network enables secure communication between all virtual machines, whereas the NAT adapter provides internet connectivity for software installation and updates.  Explanation  To perform the practical activities of Week 1, a virtual cybersecurity laboratory was  designed using VMware Workstation. The architecture consisted of three main systems connected through VMware virtual networking to simulate a small Security Operations Center \(SOC\) environment. Each machine had a specific role in the overall setup, allowing communication, monitoring, and security analysis within an isolated network.  The Ubuntu virtual machine served as the Wazuh SIEM server and acted as the central  management system. It was responsible for collecting logs, processing security events,  and displaying monitoring information through the Wazuh Dashboard. Since all security- related data was forwarded to this server, it became the core component of the entire lab  environment.  The Windows machine was configured as a monitored endpoint by installing the Wazuh  Agent. This agent continuously collected system logs and security events and securely  transmitted them to the Wazuh server. These events were later analyzed through the  Wazuh Dashboard to observe endpoint activities and detect potential security issues.  Kali Linux was deployed as the security testing machine. It was used to perform various  networking and security-related activities such as network scanning, connectivity testing,  and generating traffic that could be monitored by the Wazuh server. This allowed practical  observation of how security events are generated and recorded inside a SIEM environment.  The networking environment was configured using two VMware virtual adapters. The NAT  adapter provided internet connectivity for downloading software packages, updates, and  dependencies. The Host-Only adapter created an isolated internal network that enabled  secure communication between Ubuntu, Kali Linux, and the Windows machine without  exposing the laboratory environment to the external network.  As a result, all three systems were able to communicate successfully while maintaining a  controlled and secure testing environment suitable for cybersecurity experimentation.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 944 0 R
/Next 994 0 R
>>
