/Title (Network Configuration  VirtualNetworkConfiguration  Toestablish communication between all systems in the cybersecurity lab, VMware Workstation was configured using two virtual network adapters: NAT and Host-Only. This configuration provided internet connectivity for downloading software packages while also creating an isolated internal network for secure communication between the virtual machines.  The NAT adapter was primarily used to provide internet access to both Ubuntu and Kali  Linux. This allowed the systems to install updates, download required packages, and  access online repositories during software installation.  The Host-Only adapter created a private network that connected Ubuntu, Kali Linux, and  the Windows host. This isolated network enabled secure communication between all  machines without exposing the laboratory environment to the external network. Since  Wazuh relies on continuous communication between the server and its agents, the Host- Only network played a crucial role in the successful deployment of the monitoring  infrastructure.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 991 0 R
/Next 996 0 R
>>
