/Title (Ubuntu Network Configuration  The Ubuntu virtual machinewasconfigured with two network interfaces, each serving a different purpose.  The ens33 interface was connected to the NAT network and obtained its IP address  automatically through DHCP. This interface provided internet connectivity required for  installing the Wazuh platform and downloading software packages.  The ens34 interface was connected to the Host-Only network. Initially, it also received an  IP address through DHCP; however, to ensure consistent communication with the Wazuh  agents, it was later configured with a static IP address. Assigning a static IP ensured that  the Windows and Kali agents could always communicate with the Wazuh server using the  same address.  The network configuration was verified using the ip a and ip route commands to  confirm that both interfaces were active and correctly configured)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 994 0 R
