998 0 obj
<<
/Title (Kali Linux Network Configuration  The Kali Linuxvirtual machine was also configured with two network adapters.  The first interface was connected to the NAT network to provide internet access, while the  second interface was connected to the Host-Only network for communication with the  Ubuntu Wazuh server.  Unlike the Ubuntu server, Kali Linux continued using dynamically assigned IP addresses  because it was only functioning as a monitored endpoint and testing machine. A static IP  configuration was not required for the objectives of this lab.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 996 0 R
/Next 1001 0 R
>>
endobj
999 0 obj
<<
/Title (Verification of Connected Agents  Afterconfiguringbothendpoints,theWazuh Dashboard was used to verify their connection status. The dashboard displayed both the Windows and Kali Linux agents as Active, confirming successful enrollment and continuous communication withthe Wazuh Manager.)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1002 0 R
/Next 997 0 R
>>
