1002 0 obj
<<
/Title (Starting the Wazuh Agent on Windows  Following theinstallationof theWazuh agent on the Windows system, the Windows Service Manager was used to verify that the Wazuh service was running correctly. The command output confirmed that the service had already been started, indicating that the agent was active and functioning properly.  With the service running successfully, the Windows endpoint was able to send logs and  security events to the Wazuh server for centralized monitoring.)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1004 0 R
/Next 999 0 R
>>
endobj
1003 0 obj
<<
/Title (Network Connectivity Verification  After completing the networkconfiguration, connectivity tests were performed between Ubuntu, Kali Linux, and the Windows host using the ICMP Ping utility.  The test results confirmed successful communication between Ubuntu and Kali Linux, as  well as between the Windows host and both virtual machines. This verified that the Host- Only network was functioning correctly and that all systems were able to exchange data  before deploying the Wazuh monitoring platform.  These successful connectivity tests ensured that the environment was fully prepared for  packet analysis using Wireshark and for the deployment of the Wazuh SIEM infrastructure.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1001 0 R
/Next 1005 0 R
>>
endobj
